From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0760: scaled_copy_levers: resolve_dual_write, swap_direct_present and tonemap_transfer_skip at a draw resolution scale above 1 (Direct3D 12; native stream R1)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream, R1 of docs/native/ROADMAP.md; design note scratch/r1/DESIGN.md). Written at first without a
  build or a run (checked with clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of the 5 changed translation units and 12 that include the
  changed headers), then built and run (below). The 8 DXBC headers (src/graphics/shaders/bytecode/d3d12_5_1/resolve_direct_batched_*_scaled_dual_origin_cs.h) are built by
  Renan's launcher/dev/build_resolve_shaders.py from xenia-project/xenia 0b2ffa3, fxc 10.0.26100.0 cs_5_1 /O3 (scratch/r1/make_r1_shaders.ps1);
  built and run on 2026-11-27 (RTX 4060 laptop, 2000p ultra, fullscreen, quick_drive; the build of series 0755..0760 had no error):
  resolve_dual_write_verify=30 (run r1-ver, bit 1): about 8,450 textures compared in 11 windows (msaa about 4,000, partial about 170),
  0 differing bytes, no MISMATCH; 17,000 to 26,500 dual-written resolves per 10 s (44 a frame; 51.8 fell back `scaled` before).
  swap_direct_present_check=60 with swap_post_effect=none (run r1-sw2, bits 2 + 4): 111 checks, 0 pixels differ outside the first row
  and column of host pixels, 5,199 pixels (row 0 + column 0 of 3200x2000) differ by up to 1023 in 10 bits in 100 of them: the
  front buffer's resolve fills the half-pixel gap in this game, so bit 2 alone never engages and bit 4 leaves a one-pixel stripe along
  the top and left edge (run r1-px: green / magenta there): NOT exact. tonemap_transfer_skip_poison + skip_overwritten_transfers_poison
  (run r1-px9, bits 1 + 8): 298 of 299 tone maps a 10 s window skipped (0 kept; r1-a0 kept all), 0 magenta pixels in 29 screenshots,
  edge rows equal. Paired A/B in two saturated runs (r1-ab1, r1-ab2, gpu_experiment_cycle, 8 cycles each entry against its own
  cycle's levers 0), GPU busy of 11.8 ms: bit 1 -1.15 +- 0.09 ms (resolve + texload 4.0 -> 2.8 ms), bit 8 -0.2 ms (tone map group
  0.89 -> 0.70; -0.04 +- 0.13 on the frame alone), 9 -1.35 +- 0.18, bits 2 + 4 -0.17 +- 0.23 (swap group 0.68 -> 0.50), 15 -1.45 +- 0.25.
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: At draw scale 2 (profile 2000p: 1600x1000 guest, every render target 2x2) the copy-avoiding levers of the 1x work are
  refused or silently dead: the dual write (0490/0530: `kScaled` at render_target_cache.cpp:1858, no scaled shaders, the texture
  index holds only resolved_unscaled ones), the direct present (04a0: GetSwapTextureInfo, NoteSwapDirectResolve, and a picture size
  that would be the fetch constant's, not the scaled one) and the tone map's transfer skip (04e0: the half-pixel offset leaves the
  first host pixel of the first guest row and column of the tone map's quad uncovered, so its whole-screen test fails).
  New cvar scaled_copy_levers (int, 0..15, default 0 = the old behaviour everywhere; hot reload; no effect at scale 1), bits:
    1  resolve_dual_write / resolve_dual_write_msaa at a scale above 1: the direct resolve also writes the scaled texture the game
       samples (a scaled_resolve texture of the cache), so it isn't loaded from the scaled resolve buffer; the buffer is written
       as before (unscaled copy of resolve_unscaled_copy_rules, vinyl readback, every other texture over the range read it);
       8 new XeSL wrappers (resolve_direct_batched_{fast,full}_{32,64}bpp_{,msaa_}scaled_dual_origin.cs.xesl: XE_RESOLVE_RESOLUTION_SCALED
       with the dual write and its texel origin; resolve_direct.xesli is untouched), the dual constants in host texels
    2  swap_direct_present at a scale above 1 when the front buffer's resolve did not fill the half-pixel gap
    4  (with 2) also when it did: the picture's first host row and column are then the render target's own
    8  tonemap_transfer_skip: the tone map's quad counts as the whole screen when only the half-pixel gap isn't covered
  resolve_dual_write_verify compares the scaled texture with a scaled load (host texels; the current scaled resolve range is put back);
  swap_direct_present_check adds a line with the differences outside the first row and column; the 10 s [resolve-dual-write] line
  ends with ", scaled 2x2: N"; `fallback scaled` is given only with bit 1 off.
Bucket: REDO

0760-scaled-dual-write-direct-present.patch (mcla-x86 native stream R1).

